Rules:
  [T1] Use NestJS for structured enterprise applications.
  [T2] Use Clean Architecture with dependency inversion.
  [T3] Use DDD patterns (Entity, Value Object, Repository).
  [T4] Use CQRS for complex domain logic.
  [T5] Use Event Sourcing for audit trails.
  [T6] Use message brokers (Kafka/NATS) for async communication.
  [T7] Implement distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry.
  [T8] Use containerization (Docker) for deployment.

Pros:
  - Scalable architecture
  - Type safety at scale
  - Full-stack consistency

Cons:
  - Operational complexity
  - Learning curve
  - Tooling overhead

Alternatives:
  - Go (simpler, faster)
  - Java (enterprise standard)

State: +

